{
  "name": "WhatsApp Wholesale Shoe Sales Call Tracker",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup checklist\n1. **WhatsApp Trigger** – connect your WhatsApp Business Cloud API credential (needs `messages` webhook subscription).\n2. **HTTP Request nodes (media)** – connect an HTTP Header Auth credential with `Authorization: Bearer <your WhatsApp permanent access token>`.\n3. **OpenAI nodes** – connect your OpenAI credential (used for voice-note transcription + extracting the client's requirement/interest as structured data).\n4. **Google Sheets nodes** – connect your Google Sheets credential and point all 3 Sheets nodes at ONE spreadsheet with two tabs:\n   - `Sales Call Log` columns: Date | Time | Client Name | Phone Number | Location | Sequence No | Message Type | Message | Product Interest | Quantity/Requirement | Interest Level | Follow-up Needed | Summary | WA Message ID\n   - `Client Master` columns: Phone Number | Client Name | Location | Last Contact Date | Last Product Interest | Interest Level | Status\n5. **Gmail node** – set the \"To\" address to wherever you want hot-lead alerts sent (defaults to your email, change as needed).\n6. Send yourself a test WhatsApp message, then open each node's output once to confirm field names match the live payload (Meta tweaks these occasionally) before going live.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "sticky-setup",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-680, -420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## How the \"sequence\" works\nEach message from a client is looked up against the `Sales Call Log` tab (filtered by phone number) to count how many calls/messages already exist for them, then stamps the new row with the next Sequence No. Combined with Date/Time, this gives you a full chronological history per client.\n\nAdd this formula to `Client Master!<TotalCalls column>` if you want a live running total instead of trusting n8n:\n`=COUNTIF('Sales Call Log'!D:D, A2)` (assuming Phone Number is column D in the log and column A in Client Master).",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "sticky-sequence",
      "name": "Sequence Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [560, -420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": ["messages"]
      },
      "id": "node-trigger",
      "name": "WhatsApp Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.whatsAppTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-680, 0],
      "webhookId": "whatsapp-sales-tracker",
      "credentials": {
        "whatsAppTriggerApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "WhatsApp Business Cloud account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": { "caseSensitive": true, "leftValue": "", "typeValidation": "strict" },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.type }}",
                    "rightValue": "text",
                    "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              }
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": { "caseSensitive": true, "leftValue": "", "typeValidation": "strict" },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.type }}",
                    "rightValue": "audio",
                    "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              }
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": { "caseSensitive": true, "leftValue": "", "typeValidation": "strict" },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.type }}",
                    "rightValue": "location",
                    "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "fallbackOutput": 3,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-switch",
      "name": "Route by Message Type",
